# React function components

Define React components as typed function components (`FC`), not untyped `function` declarations. Give props a named `interface` — do not inline the props object type on the parameter.

Pure helpers that do not return JSX stay as `function` declarations with explicit parameter and return types.

Leave generated shadcn files in `components/ui/` as the CLI produced them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — untyped function, inline props
function ProjectLink({ label, href }: { label: string; href: string }) {
  return <a href={href}>{label}</a>
}

// ✅ GOOD
interface ProjectLinkProps {
  label: string
  href: string
}

const ProjectLink: FC<ProjectLinkProps> = ({ label, href }) => {
  return <a href={href}>{label}</a>
}
```

- Import `FC` as a type: `import { type FC } from "react"`
- Components with no props: `const Projects: FC = () => { ... }`
- Declare `children` on the props interface when the component accepts them — do not rely on implicit `children`
- Named exports for reusable UI; default export for page sections (`components/home.tsx`, etc.) and route files
- Async Server Component routes stay `export default async function` — do not convert those to `FC`
